   "title": "Boeing, 747-400 Airplane Characteristics for Airport Planning (D6-58326-1 Rev F, December 2024), 2.2.1 General Dimensions: Model 747-400, and 2.7.1 Door Locations",
   "accessed": "2026-11-15",
   "note": "The fuselage, upper deck, fin, tailplane, doors, cockpit and main-deck windows are the 747-400's measured outlines (shapes/B744-passenger.json, tools/trace/b744-passenger/) with the 747-8's two plugs (tools/trace/b748-passenger/derive.py). Its 2.7.1 figure puts the upper deck's fairing end 1.53 m ahead of door 3's middle, as its general-dimensions sheet does."
  },
  {
   "url": "https://www.boeing.com/content/dam/boeing/boeingdotcom/commercial/airports/acaps/747-8_Rev_E.pdf",
   "title": "Boeing, 747-8 Airplane Characteristics for Airport Planning (D6-58326-3 Rev E, January 2026), 2.2.2 General Dimensions: Model 747-8, and 2.7.1 Door Locations",
   "accessed": "2026-11-15",
   "note": "Low-resolution binarized scans, too coarse to trace: the plugs from the door table (doors 2 and 3 4.1 m, doors 4 and 5 5.6 m further back than the 747-400's; 74.22 m nose to tail cone), the wing and GEnx-2B nacelles as the 747-8F's (shapes/B748.json), and the upper deck read off both side views: 4.10 m longer than the 747-400's (its cabin's end 6.8 m behind door 2 on both types), its fairing running out about 1 m further aft (to 34.3 m, 0.47 m ahead of door 3 on 2.7.1). 2.2.2's side view draws door 3 about 3.5 m forward of the table's 34.7 m, which 2.7.1's figure doesn't: the table's kept. Neither scan's windows can be placed or counted to a window (about 8 px a meter): those are from the photos. Confidence medium for the scans and photos."
  },
  {
   "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:D-ABYS_AIRCRAFT_Boeing_747-830_-1e.jpg",
   "title": "Sg1959, D-ABYS AIRCRAFT Boeing 747-830 -1e, 2026-06-20 (Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 4.0)",
   "accessed": "2026-11-15",
   "note": "Upper-deck windows and door, and a check of the main deck's: each one's middle along the cabin (left side, side-on from below), scaled by a perspective fit to the visible main doors' windows (doors 1, 2, 4 and 5 at the door table's figures). Only measurements are taken; nothing of the photo is copied."
  },
  {
